jobs.description:
As a Control Panel Builder, you will assemble and wire electrical control panels according to technical drawings and electrical schematics. You make sure that each panel is completed safely, accurately, and in line with the customer’s requirements.

Your daily responsibilities include:

- Assembling control cabinets and operator panels;
- Mounting and wiring electrical components;
- Reading and working from electrical drawings and schematics;
- Checking and testing completed control panels;
- Occasionally supporting installation or service work at customer locations.

Most of your work will take place in the workshop, where you will work alongside a team of experienced technicians.

- Technical MBO diploma in Electrical Engineering or related field;
- Experience with control panel assembly is a plus;
- Ability to work from technical and electrical drawings;
- Detail-oriented and quality-focused mindset;
- Able to work independently and in a team;
- English communication skills required.

Sharp and administrative talent wanted in Rotterdam (Maasvlakte II)!



Are you a proactive and driven inspector with a keen eye for detail? Do you also have a passion for administration and are you efficient at streamlining processes? Then we're looking for you!

What are you going to do?
As a Gate Inspector, you are responsible for:

- Access control: You are the first point of contact for drivers and ensure smooth and safe access to the site.
- Accurate administration: You handle all administrative processes related to the containers, from scheduling to invoicing.
- Damage control: You inspect the containers for damage, cleanliness, and claims, and report these accurately.

What do we offer?
- A gross hourly salary of €18,18 - €20.65 based on experience;
- 14% allowence for each hour worked;
- €0.23 mileage allowance;
- Two-shift system, Monday through Friday (5:45 AM - 2:00 PM / 1:45 PM - 10:00 PM);
- A contract through Adecco;
- 8.33% holiday allowance and 25 vacation days (full-time);
- Pension accrual from your first day of work;
- Personal development: During your contract, you have access to the Adecco Academy, offering online training and courses.

Where will you work?
Maersk is everywhere, from a road trip alongside one of our trucks to the world's largest ports where we arrive and continue our journey to your doorstep. Now's your chance to get to know us from the inside out: a workplace filled with warmth, friendship, and support. We invite you to join our incredible team and be part of our purpose: improving life for everyone by inspiring the world!

What do we ask?
- Previous education/work experience in administration is required;
- Knowledge of business systems is a plus;
- You can work independently and as part of a team;
- Proper handling of common tasks;
- VCA basic certification is a plus;
- A wilingness to obtain (VOG) is required;
- The own transport (car) is required;
- English and communicative Dutch is required

Are you interested?
